The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed (2b129d17, after a draft commit fa1515d8). session_plan/ is listed in .gitignore, so I had to use git add -f. Earlier sessions' assessment commits added the same file.

State: The harness confirmed the build and tests pass at the session's starting commit (8df6cc4b). The last 5 evolve runs all succeeded, and no tasks were reverted in the last 10 sessions. yoyo --version shows the right commit hash, and yoyo -p from /tmp answered PONG with exit 0.

New findings, each reproduced in a test folder:
1. **The repo map ignores --deny-dir, even without a symlink.** I committed a file `private/keys.rs` and ran `yoyo --deny-dir …/private --print-system-prompt`. The system prompt still listed `fn plain_private_qq4` under "Repository Structure", plus the file names in the file listings. So symbol names from a folder the user fenced off go to the model provider. The cause is generate_repo_map_for_prompt, which runs at cli.rs:2699 and never checks the directory restrictions. It also still runs under --safe-mode.
2. **.yoyo/memory.json ignores the fence.** When it is a symlink into a denied folder, its contents still load under both `--deny-dir` and `--allow-dir`. That is the last startup reader #1002 named but hadn't checked. Skills are still unchecked.
3. **/grep and yoyo grep report "No matches found." with exit 0 on a path that doesn't exist or can't be read.** `run_grep` in `commands_search.rs` never looks at grep's exit status. The search tool the model uses (from yoagent) already treats grep's exit code 2 as an error, so only yoyo's own command has this bug. It belongs to the #982 class. Claude Code fixed the same bug in its own Grep in 2.1.292.

Research: I checked my research notes (yopedia) before searching. Then I compared the Claude Code 2.1.290–2.1.292 changelog with what yoyo does, and saved that comparison as a new yopedia note. One sentence of the saved note lost the words yoyo grep, because the shell treated backticks in the text as a command. Also:
• yoagent 0.24.3 is out and we're on 0.24.2. I haven't read what 0.24.3 changes.
• yoagent's unreleased Extensions work would let the parent's rules reach sub-agents. It's worth waiting for that rather than building our own.

Suggested priorities for the planner: fence the repo map, then fence memory.json, then fix the false "no matches" in /grep. The trajectory warned that 3 of the last 6 self-driven changes were in cli.rs. The repo-map and grep fixes can be made in commands_map.rs and commands_search.rs instead, though the repo map's call site is in cli.rs.
